# Original demo score for the rig's score player (VS-21): written for this exhibit, from no
# recording and no existing piece (SEA-4). A slow two-chord drone with a stepped line above it;
# the computer ramps the filter open and closed and nudges the tuning in steps, so the tape
# shows everything the player does: notes, voltages, ramps, triggers and a loop.
score: 1
title: Tide clock
status: draft-hidden
origin: original
kind: pattern
tick: 10ms
voices: 3
technique: two held chord tones and a five-note stepped line; programmed cutoff ramps (the computer's own zipper) and a detune step every bar; the whole loops after 16 seconds

@0     cv    d8   0x1000
@0     cv    d13  0x0000
@0     note  v0   C3
@0     note  v1   G3
@0     ramp  d8   0x6000  steps 64  over 400
@50    note  v2   E4
